{"seq":1,"ts":"2026-11-07T13:10:08.130Z","type":"exp.start","exp":"E-ONGOING-01","attempt":1,"title":"Ongoing groups on testnet: a Dark Vault that lives across three rounds with three programs, takes a late deposit, and what its release cap really bounds","tier":"testnet","hypothesis":"Predictions are fixed in docs/lab/PROGRAMME_PLAN.md (committed before this ran). A. Four members deposit 0.1 each into a Dark Vault (25% cap, 16-block exit timer); round 1 an investing pool (0.05 to rp); a fifth member deposits 0.1; round 2 a ballot among all five (0.05 to ra); round 3 a lending quote (0.04 to rl, won by u3 at 400 bps). (1) The epoch rises by exactly 1 per settlement and the round nonce changes each time. (2) The late member joins between rounds and is counted and charged correctly; escrows sum to the group total after every round. (3) Replaying round 1's signed settlement after round 2 is refused and changes nothing. (4) The exit timer restarts each epoch: an exit right after round 3 is refused; 16 blocks after the last settlement every member exits alone with exactly deposit minus charges (u1 0.08, u2 0.08, u3 0.035, u4 0.075, u5 0.09). B. With a key we hold standing in for a compromised host, a payout above 25% of the current escrow is refused, but payouts of exactly 25% of the current escrow succeed back to back (0.1, 0.075, 0.05625), releasing 0.23125 of 0.4, which is 57.8% against a stated 25% per epoch: expected to be a design weakness. Fails if A breaks; B is recorded as a finding if it holds.","limits":["One operator controls every account and the host; the members are scripted. The host is a local HostedRoost with a simulated attestation provider; signed inputs use real NEAR keys and the real account-key lookup.","Three rounds and five members: not a long-lived or large group. There is no baseline; this tests the contract's lifecycle claims against what it says.","Part B uses a key we hold to stand in for a compromised host, because a real host refuses to sign more than it computed.","Only the cash leg settles. Deposits are public."],"requires":["near-key","network"],"chain_prev":"32929f159e50465eb40666888e7d963eed97abe569cb0db500de736f30eafa55","chain_hash":"cc7a5944973b6ef87cbef9550ed227f9839e745decdf10b9580a02865c97e22f"}
